course: dictionary
lesson: 6837
title: The outside and the inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Outer means on the outside, the part farthest from the middle. When you meet it, ask: is this thing on the edge, or deep in the middle? Think of a hard-boiled egg: the shell is the outer part, and the yolk is the inside.
explain: «The outer core is liquid iron and nickel, and its swirling makes the Earth's magnetic field.» The clue is the word core. A core is the middle, and outer tells you this layer sits around the middle, not in it. It helps to look for its partner word, inner, in the next sentence: «The inner core is a solid ball of iron and nickel.»
explain: Outer also shows up in phrases like outer space and outer edge. «Insects and spiders have no backbone; they have a hard outer skeleton.» The skeleton is on the outside of the body, where you can see and touch it. Each time you meet outer, picture where the thing is, and you will usually find the meaning.
fact: Outer means on the outside, the part farthest from the middle.
fact: Outer space is the space beyond the air around the Earth.
fact: Outer and inner are opposites: «the inner core» sits inside «the outer core».
fact: In maths, an outer border is the whole area minus the inner area.
fact: The outer layer of the Earth is the crust.
exercise: «The outer wall of the castle was thick and grey.» What does outer mean here? | Very old | Very tall | On the inside, near the middle | *On the outside, farthest from the middle
exercise: «Insects and spiders have a hard outer skeleton.» Where is the skeleton? | Inside the body | *On the outside of the body | In the head only
exercise: Which word means the opposite of outer? | Far | Blue | Hard | *Inner
test: «Skin has three main layers: the outer epidermis, the dermis with blood vessels and nerves, and a fat layer underneath.» Which layer is the outer one? | The dermis | *The epidermis | The fat layer
test: What is outer space? | *The space beyond the air around the Earth | The inside of the Earth | Air around the Earth | The sea floor
exam: Which layer of the Earth is liquid iron and nickel, and makes the magnetic field? | *The outer core | The inner core | The outer space | The crust
